# "motion" in P1 is what is evident to the senses, likely local motion. From S4 on it is change in general, any passage from potentiality to actuality. Local motion is one case of such change, so P1 is true in both senses and the claim does not divide.
# In P6, P7, P8 and P9, "first mover" is read the same way: an unmoved source on which subsequent movers depend, as the staff depends on the hand. It is not read as earliest in time anywhere in the text, so I mark it one sense.
